When Xavier is midway along its orbit, it lies on the semi-minor axis. The distance from the center of the ellipse to any point on the semi-minor axis is \(b\). Since the sun is at one focus, the distance from the sun to the point on the semi-minor axis is:
\[
\sqrt{c^2 + b^2} = \sqrt{5^2 + (2\sqrt{6})^2} = \sqrt{25 + 24} = \sqrt{49} = 7 \text{ AU}
\]

Thus, the distance from the sun to Xavier when it is midway along its orbit is \(\boxed{7}\) AU.

